WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.739 --> 00:00:02.300
this is super interesting.

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:08.879
Our old friend, Andrew Yang, who ran for the
Democratic presidential nomination this year,

00:00:08.879 --> 00:00:14.639
is already leading a poll for New York City
mayor, even though he's not running yet.

00:00:14.639 --> 00:00:18.099
And there's been a movement to draft Andrew
Yang to the New York City mayor.

00:00:18.099 --> 00:00:19.840
He's not yet a candidate.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:24.369
And among Democrats, meaning within the New
York City Democratic mayoral primary, Andrew

00:00:24.369 --> 00:00:25.369
Yang is winning.

00:00:25.369 --> 00:00:31.920
Yang is polling 17, Eric Adams polling 16,
everybody else at 10 or below.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:37.200
There's another poll from a couple of weeks
ago where it was Andrew Yang, 20, with Eric

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:42.280
Adams, who I believe is the council I believe
is the council president in New York City,

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:44.180
down at 14 percent.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:46.580
So this is the twenty, twenty one election.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:49.940
The New York City mayoral election is on November
2nd.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:51.050
Twenty twenty one.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.960
The primary is on June 22nd.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.650
So we're already only six months from the
New York City mayoral primary.

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:01.760
And in the grand scheme of things, that's
pretty soon it'll just be five months once

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.420
Joe Biden is inaugurated.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:09.950
Now, the current New York City mayor, Bill
de Blasio, is term limited from running again.

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:15.340
And this upcoming election is going to be
the first one in New York City using ranked

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:16.780
choice voting.

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:21.060
So there's a bunch of very interesting things
related to this.

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:22.060
It's very early.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:26.270
The polling is basically a tie within the
margin of error in this latest poll.

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:28.200
And Andrew Yang hasn't even announced.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.590
And that's exactly what makes this so interesting.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:36.369
Without even being a candidate, merely with
the rumor of being a candidate this early.

00:01:36.369 --> 00:01:40.759
Andrew Yang is already doing really well now
at the same time.

00:01:40.759 --> 00:01:46.649
Even though Andrew Yang is not yet running,
he has signaled that he is likely to run in

00:01:46.649 --> 00:01:47.969
a few different ways.

00:01:47.969 --> 00:01:52.619
First of all, there are lots of people claiming
they've been told privately that Andrew Yang

00:01:52.619 --> 00:01:54.920
plans to run for New York City mayor.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:02:00.810
Second, there are people saying that Andrew
Yang has actually decided to run and is simply

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:06.600
waiting for January, maybe after Joe Biden's
inauguration to make the announcement.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:09.950
But Andrew Yang has been meeting with some
important New York City figures.

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:13.860
Cory Johnson, who's speaker of the city council
to talk about running.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:18.280
He's hired as advisors, a Bradley Tusk and
Chris Coffee, who advised Michael Bloomberg

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.610
when Michael Bloomberg ran for mayor.

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:24.290
So I think this is very interesting for a
number of different reasons.

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:30.190
Number one, Andrew Yang would bring a sort
of pragmatism to the office of mayor that

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:35.580
Bill de Blasio, even for as well-intentioned
as he may be, I think lacks.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:37.390
And I think that would be a very interesting
aspect.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:43.000
You know, one of the critiques of Andrew Yang
is that as president, Andrew Yang's approach

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:51.240
of sort of like the tech CEO, consultant,
technocratic approach, that it's not well

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:53.620
suited for the president.

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:57.800
It actually may be well suited for New York
City mayor in some ways, which will dig into

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:04.111
if indeed he he announces, number two, there's
going to be many people who if Andrew Yang

00:03:04.111 --> 00:03:08.030
does announce that he's running for New York
City mayor who are going to say Andrew Yang

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:13.990
is not really progressive and there are going
to be other New Yorkers, maybe not in the

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:18.290
Democratic primary, but I'm thinking of Staten
Island Republicans who are going to say Yang

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:24.450
is a socialist because he believes in universal
basic income, which was one of his main sort

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:28.530
of distinguishing policy ideas during the
Democratic primary.

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:33.070
So you're going to have I mean, listen, it's
no different than with Biden, where the progressive

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:37.480
left says Biden is not very progressive and
the right says Biden is a socialist, communist,

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:40.440
Venezuelan, Marxist, Stalinist, whatever.

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:45.020
It'll be even further exacerbated because
this is all, you know, millions of people

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:46.870
in a very small geographical area.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:49.350
So I think the contrast will be very notable.

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:52.380
And number three, there's an interesting identity
story here as well.

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:57.550
Andrew Young would be only the second Asian-American
candidate to even run for mayor.

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:00.540
The other was John Liu in 2013.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:06.760
And then number four, because Andrew Yang
has such nationwide name recognition, it would

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:11.440
be very interesting to see how beneficial
that is in a New York City race.

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:17.759
New York City mayor is one of the least local
local races because people and companies from

00:04:17.759 --> 00:04:23.160
all over the country, even all over the world,
have a vested interest, a financial interest

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:24.160
in many cases.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:29.419
And who is mayor of New York City typically
for business related considerations?

00:04:29.419 --> 00:04:34.569
What I wonder if Andrew Yang has thought of,
and he probably has, I would imagine he has

00:04:34.569 --> 00:04:41.120
been thinking about it, is that New York City
mayor is a job where almost no matter what

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:46.780
you do, you are going to have a large swath
of New Yorkers furious with you about the

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:52.629
job that that you've done with some very rare
brief exceptions like Rudy Giuliani after

00:04:52.629 --> 00:04:53.800
9/11.

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:59.080
New York City is so diverse politically, economically,
racially, in all ways.

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:05.550
You know, from Bronx, Queens, the Manhattan
crowd, even within Manhattan, Staten Island,

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:10.580
the most conservative part of New York City,
there's a large swath of the population that's

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:13.409
almost always furious with the New York City
mayor.

00:05:13.409 --> 00:05:16.590
You are one of the most powerful local officials
in the country.

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:21.849
As New York City mayor, you run a government
larger than many states as New York City mayor.

00:05:21.849 --> 00:05:26.080
And it comes with some horrible realities
that the mayor is always being ripped apart.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:29.789
But in the end, it's not that different from
being president when half the country hates

00:05:29.789 --> 00:05:30.789
you.

00:05:30.789 --> 00:05:35.120
But geographically, again, the hate is in
a much smaller area and it's around all the

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:36.120
time.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:37.560
I'm sure Andrew Yang can handle it.

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:41.610
Every expectation is that we'll hear from
him next month about whether or not he decides

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:45.500
to run and many reports that it's a foregone
conclusion that he's running.

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:47.110
He simply is waiting to announce.

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:48.449
So let me know your thoughts.

00:05:48.449 --> 00:05:52.969
I think there were ideas of what about if
he runs for governor somewhere?

00:05:52.969 --> 00:05:56.050
What if Andrew Yang runs for Senate somewhere?

00:05:56.050 --> 00:05:58.680
But New York City mayor is very interesting.

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:01.029
And I'd be curious to hear your thoughts about
it.

